Assess the risk level of this DATA_PROTECTION clause:

"Data Protection Obligations" means, as applicable:

(a) relevant data protection regulations that apply within the United Kingdom;

(b) applicable privacy laws currently in effect or as updated;

(c) any privacy laws applicable in other regions where relevant.

"Data Subject" shall refer to an individual as defined under the Data Protection Obligations;

"Existing Sub-Processor" means a third-party to which Komainu has, at the Effective Date:

(a) delegated some aspects of the Services; and/or

(b) handled Client Personal Data,

in connection with the Services under the Agreement;

"New Sub-Processor" means a third-party, other than an Existing Sub-Processor, to whom Komainu intends to delegate the Processing of Client Personal Data;

"Personal Data" shall refer to data as defined under the Data Protection Obligations;

"Personal Data Breach" means a security lapse leading to unintended destruction, alteration, exposure of, or access to Client Personal Data;

"Processing" shall refer to the handling of data as defined under the Data Protection Obligations;

"Processing Activities" has the meaning set out in the applicable section of this appendix;

"Processor" shall refer to an entity responsible for data handling as defined under the Data Protection Obligations (and, in connection with this appendix and any Processing undertaken, shall mean Komainu unless specified otherwise);

"Restricted Transfer" means:

(a) a transfer of Client Personal Data from the Client to a Contracted Processor; or

(b) a subsequent transfer of Client Personal Data from a Contracted Processor,

where such transfer would be restricted by Data Protection Obligations unless using:

(1) necessary data transfer agreements; or

(2) other compliant mechanisms to transfer personal data outside of the relevant regions.

Assess the risk level of this TERMINATION clause:

4.1 Termination for Cause. The Corporation may terminate the employment of the Executive at any time for cause by notifying the Executive.

If the Corporation terminates the employment of the Executive for cause, the Corporation shall not be obligated to make any further payments except amounts due at the time of the termination.

4.2 Resignation by Executive. The Executive shall give the Corporation reasonable notice of the resignation and the Executive’s employment shall terminate on the date specified in the notice. Upon receipt of the Executive’s notice of resignation, the Corporation may waive the notice by paying the Executive’s salary for the remainder of the notice period and a reasonable amount in lieu of benefits, and if the Corporation so elects, the Executive’s employment shall terminate earlier.

4.3 Termination Without Cause. The Corporation may terminate the Executive’s employment at any time without cause by giving the Executive notice and the following entitlements:

(a) the Corporation shall pay the Executive all outstanding and accrued base salary and vacation pay, earned and owing up to the last day of employment, and shall reimburse the Executive for all reasonable expenses incurred in connection with the Corporation’s business prior to the last day of employment;

(b) the Corporation shall pay the Executive an amount equal to a reasonable period of base salary;

(c) the Corporation shall pay the Executive an amount in lieu of the Executive’s performance bonus as agreed;

(d) the Corporation shall continue the Executive’s benefit coverage for a period as agreed, or alternatively, if it is unable to continue the Executive’s participation in one or more of its benefit plans, the Corporation shall pay the Executive an amount equal to the premium cost or contributions the Corporation would otherwise have made;

(e) The Corporation shall have the option of making the payments required either in lump sum or in instalments as agreed;

